献者知道实施该API合理所需的专利许可，则贡献者还必须在法律文件中包含此信息。\n\n(A)第三方索赔。如果贡献者知道需要第三方知识产权下的许可证才能行使该贡献者根据第2.1或2.2节授予的权利，则贡献者必须包括一个标题为“Legal”的源代码分发的文本文件，该文件详细描述了索赔和提出索赔的一方，以便收件人知道联系谁。如果贡献者在第3.2节所述的修改可用后获得此类知识，则贡献者应立即修改贡献者此后提供的所有副本中的法律文件，并应采取合理的其他步骤(例如通知适当的邮件列表或新闻组)，以告知收到所涵盖代码的人新的知识S已经获得。\n\n(C)申述。贡献者声明，除根据上述第3.4(A)节披露的情况外，贡献者认为贡献者的修改是贡献者的原创作品(S)和/或贡献者有足够的权利授予本许可证所传达的权利。\n\n3.5.所需的通知。您必须在源代码的每个文件中复制附件A中的通知。如果由于其结构原因，无法将此类通知放入特定源代码文件中，则您必须在用户可能会查找此类通知的位置(如相关目录)中包含此类通知。如果您创建了一项或多项修改(S)，您可以将您的姓名作为贡献者添加到附件A中描述的通知中。您还必须在描述接受者权利或与所涵盖代码相关的所有权的任何源代码文档中复制本许可证。您可以选择向所涵盖代码的一个或多个收件人提供保修、支持、赔偿或责任义务，并收取费用。但是，您只能代表您自己这样做，而不能代表最初的开发者或任何贡献者。您必须绝对明确，任何此类保证、支持、赔偿或责任义务都是由您单独提供的，并且您在此同意赔偿初始开发者和每个贡献者因您提供的保证、支持、赔偿或责任条款而产生的任何责任。\n\n3.6.可执行版本的分发。您只能以可执行形式分发所涵盖的代码，前提是该所涵盖的代码已满足第3.1-3.5节的要求，并且您包括一份声明，声明所涵盖的代码的源代码版本可根据本许可证的条款提供，其中包括对您如何以及在何处履行第3.2节的义务的描述。该通知必须显眼地包括在以下任何通知中可执行版本、相关文档或宣传品，您在其中描述收件人与所涵盖代码相关的权利。您可以根据您选择的许可证分发所涵盖代码的可执行版本或所有权，该许可证可能包含与本许可证不同的条款，前提是您遵守本许可证的条款，并且可执行版本的许可证不试图限制或更改接受者在源代码版本中的权利，而不是本许可证中规定的权利。如果您在不同的许可证下分发可执行版本，您必须绝对明确，任何与本许可证不同的条款都是由您单独提供的，而不是由初始开发者或任何贡献者提供。您在此同意赔偿初始开发者和每个贡献者因您提供的任何此类条款而产生的任何责任。\n\n3.7.更大的作品。您可以通过将所涵盖的代码与不受本许可证条款管辖的其他代码相结合来创建较大的作品，并将较大的作品作为单个产品分发。在这种情况下，您必须确保所涵盖代码满足本许可证的要求。\n\n4.因法规或规章而不能遵守的。\n\n如果由于法规、司法命令或法规的原因，您无法就所涵盖的部分或全部代码遵守本许可证的任何条款，则您必须：(A)最大限度地遵守本许可证的条款；以及(B)描述限制及其影响的代码。此类描述必须包含在3.4节中描述的法律文件中，并且必须包含在源代码的所有分发版本中。除法规或条例禁止的范围外，此类描述必须足够详细，使普通技术人员能够理解。\n\n5.本许可证的适用范围。\n\n本许可证适用于INITIAL开发商已在附件A和相关涵盖代码中附上了该通知。\n\n6.许可证的版本。\n\n6.2.新版本的效果。所涵盖的代码在许可证的特定版本下发布后，您可以始终根据该版本的条款继续使用它。您也可以选择根据SugarCRM发布的许可证的任何后续版本的条款使用此类所涵盖的代码。除SugarCRM外，任何人都无权修改适用于根据本许可证创建的所涵盖代码的条款。\n\n6.3.衍生作品。如果您创建或使用本许可证的修改版本(您这样做可能只是为了将其应用于不受本许可证管辖的代码)，您必须(A)重命名您的许可证，使“SugarCRM”、“SPL”或任何令人困惑的相似短语不会出现在您的许可证中(注意您的许可证与本许可证不同)，以及(B)以其他方式明确您的许可证版本包含与SugarCRM公共许可证不同的条款。(在附件A中描述的通知中填写初始开发者、原始代码或贡献者的名称本身不应被视为对本许可证的修改。)\n\n7.免责声明。\n\n根据本许可证，所涵盖的代码是按原样提供的，不提供任何明示或默示的担保，包括但不限于对所涵盖的代码没有缺陷、可销售、适合特定用途或不侵权的担保。有关所涵盖代码的质量和性能的全部风险由您承担。如果任何所涵盖的代码被证明在任何方面有缺陷，您(不是最初的开发者或任何其他贡献者)承担任何必要的服务、修复或更正的费用。本免责声明是本许可证的重要组成部分。除本免责声明外，不得在本协议下授权使用任何所涵盖的代码。\n\n8.终止。\n\n8.2.如果你发起通过对初始开发者或贡献者(您向其提起诉讼的初始开发者或贡献者称为“参与者”)主张专利侵权索赔(不包括解密判决诉讼)而提起的诉讼：\n\n(A)该参与者的贡献人版本直接或间接侵犯了任何专利，则该参与者根据本许可证第2.1和/或2.2节向您授予的任何和所有权利应在参与者发出60天通知后预期终止，除非您在收到通知后60天内：(I)书面同意就您过去和将来使用该参与者所做的修改向参与者支付双方同意的合理版税，或(Ii)撤回您针对该参与者就贡献人版本提出的诉讼要求。如果在通知的60天内，双方未以书面形式就合理的特许权使用费和付款安排达成一致，或诉讼索赔未被撤回，则参与者根据第2.1条和/或2.2条授予您的权利将在上述60天通知期限届满时自动终止。\n\n(B)除该参与者的贡献者版本之外的任何软件、硬件或设备直接或间接侵犯了任何专利，则该参与者根据第2.1(B)和2.2(B)条授予您的任何权利自您首次对该参与者所做的修改进行、使用、销售、分发或已经做出修改之日起被撤销。\n\n8.3.如果您对参与者提出专利侵权索赔，声称该参与者的贡献者版本直接或间接侵犯了任何专利，并且在发起专利侵权诉讼之前此类索赔已得到解决(例如通过许可或和解)，则在确定任何付款人的金额或价值时，应考虑该参与者根据第2.1或2.2条授予的许可的合理价值T或许可证。\n\n8.4.如果根据上述条款8.1或8.2终止，您或任何分销商在终止前在本协议项下有效授予的所有最终用户许可协议(不包括分销商和经销商)在终止后仍然有效。\n\n9.责任限制。\n\n在任何情况下，根据任何法律理论，无论侵权(包括疏忽)、合同或其他，您、初始开发者、任何其他贡献者、所涵盖代码的任何分发者或任何此等各方的任何供应商，都不对任何人承担任何间接、特殊、附带或后果性的损害，包括但不限于商誉损失、停工、计算机故障或故障的损害，或任何和所有其他商业损害或损失，即使此方已被告知此类损害的可能性。在适用法律禁止的范围内，这一责任限制不适用于该当事人的疏忽造成的死亡或人身伤害的责任。某些司法管辖区不允许排除或限制附带或后果性损害，因此此排除和限制可能不适用于您。\n\n10.美国政府终端用户。\n\n按照48C.F.R.2.101(1995年10月)中对该术语的定义，所涵盖的代码是“商业项目”，包括“商业计算机软件”和“商业计算机软件文档”，如第48 C.F.R.12.212(2015年9月)中所使用的术语。1995年)。根据48 C.F.R.227.7202-1至227.7202-4(1995年6月)的48 C.F.R.12.212和48 C.F.R.12.212，所有美国政府最终用户获得的承保代码仅包含本文所述的权利。\n\n11.杂项。\n\n本许可证代表与本协议主题相关的完整协议。如果本许可证的任何条款被认为是不可执行的，应仅在使其可执行所需的范围内对该条款进行改革。本许可证应受加州法律规定的管辖NS(除非适用法律另有规定)，不包括其法律冲突条款。对于至少一方是美国公民或被特许或注册在美利坚合众国开展业务的实体的纠纷，任何与本许可证有关的诉讼应受加利福尼亚州北区联邦法院的管辖，诉讼地点位于加利福尼亚州圣克拉拉县，败诉方负责费用，包括但不限于法院费用和合理的律师费和开支。《联合国国际货物销售合同公约》的适用被明确排除在外。任何规定合同语言应被解释为对起草人不利的法律或法规不适用于本许可证。\n\n12.索赔责任。\n\n在初始开发者和贡献者之间，每一方都对因使用本许可证下的权利而直接或间接产生的索赔和损害负责，您同意与初始开发者和贡献者合作，在公平的基础上分配此类责任。本协议没有任何意图，也不应被视为构成任何责任的承认。\n\n13.多许可代码。\n\n初始开发者可将所涵盖代码的某些部分指定为“多重许可”。“多重许可”是指初始开发者允许您根据您选择的SPL或初始开发者在附件A中描述的文件中指定的替代许可证(如果有)使用所涵盖代码的一部分。\n\nSugarCRM公共许可证1.1.3-附件A\n\n此文件的内容受SugarCRM公共许可证版本1.1.3(“许可证”)的约束；除非遵守许可证，否则您不能使用此文件。您可以从http://www.sugarcrm.com/SPL获取许可证的副本。根据许可证分发的软件是按原样分发的，不提供任何担保。F任何一种，明示或默示。有关许可证下管理权利和限制的特定语言，请参阅许可证。\n\n原始代码是：SugarCRM开源\n\n原始代码的最初开发者是SugarCRM，Inc.\nSugarCRM创建的部分版权所有(C)2004 SugarCRM，Inc.；\n版权所有。\n撰稿人(S)：_。\n\n[注：本附件A的文本可能与原始代码源代码文件中的通知文本略有不同。您应使用本附件A的文本进行修改，而不是使用原始代码源代码中的文本。]\n\nSugarCRM公共许可证1.1.3-附件B\n\n适用于SugarCRM公共许可证的其他条款。\n\nI.效果。\n本SugarCRM公共许可证中描述的这些附加条款-附加条款应适用于本许可证所涵盖的代码。\n\nII.SugarCRM和标志。\n本许可证不授予使用商标“SugarCRM”和“SugarCRM”徽标的任何权利，即使这些标记包含在原始代码或修改中。\n\n但是，除其他通知义务外，作为原始作者的一种归属形式，所有分发的可执行和源代码形式的所涵盖代码的副本必须在每个用户界面屏幕上包括(I)“Powered by SugarCRM”徽标和(Ii)与SugarCRM，Inc.在分发该副本时分发的所涵盖代码的最新版本相同形式的版权声明。此外，“Powered by SugarCRM”徽标必须对所有用户可见，并且位于每个用户界面屏幕的最底部中心。尽管如此，“Powered by SugarCRM”标识的尺寸必须至少为106 x 23像素。当用户点击“Powered by SugarCRM”徽标时，它必须将他们定向回http://www.sugarforge.org.此外，版权声明必须始终在用户界面屏幕底部对所有用户可见。当我们ERS点击版权声明，必须将他们定向回http://www.sugarcrm.com', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (252, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'NLPL', 'No Limit Public License', 'https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Licensing/NLPL', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> NO LIMIT PUBLIC LICENSE\n\nVersion 0, June 2012<<endOptional>><<beginOptional>> Gilles LAMIRAL\n\nLa Billais\n\n35580 Baulon\n\nFrance<<endOptional>><<beginOptional>> NO LIMIT PUBLIC LICENSE<<endOptional>>\n\nTerms and conditions for copying, distribution, modification or anything else.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"0.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> No limit to do anything with this work and this license.', 'NO LIMIT PUBLIC LICENSE\n     Version 0, June 2012\n\nGilles LAMIRAL\nLa Billais\n35580 Baulon\nFrance\n\nNO LIMIT PUBLIC LICENSE\n\nTerms and conditions for copying, distribution, modification\nor anything else.\n\n     0. No limit to do anything with this work and this license.', '无限制公共许可\n版本0,2012年6月\n\n吉勒斯·拉米勒\nLa Billais\n宝龙35580\n法国\n\n无限制公共许可\n\n复制、分发、修改的条款和条件\n或者其他任何事情。\n\n0。不限制使用本作品和本许可证进行任何操作。', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (253, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'SGI-B-1.1', 'SGI Free Software License B v1.1', 'http://oss.sgi.com/projects/FreeB/', 0, 0, 0, 0, 'License Applicability. Except to the extent portions of this file are made subject to an alternative license as permitted in the SGI Free Software License B, Version 1.1 (the \"License\"), the contents of this file are subject only to the provisions of the License. You may not use this file except in compliance with the License. You may obtain a copy of the License at Silicon Graphics, Inc., attn: Legal Services, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043-1351, or at:\n\nhttp://oss.sgi.com/projects/FreeB\n\nNote that, as provided in the License, the Software is distributed on an \"AS IS\" basis, with ALL EXPRESS AND IMPLIED WARRANTIES AND CONDITIONS DISCLAIMED, INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, ANY IMPLIED WARRANTIES AND CONDITIONS OF MERCHANTABILITY, SATISFACTORY QUALITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.\n\nOriginal Code. The Original Code is: [ name of software , version number , and release date] , developed by Silicon Graphics, Inc. The Original Code is Copyright (c) [ dates of first publication, as appearing in the Notice in the Original Code] Silicon Graphics, Inc. Copyright in any portions created by third parties is as indicated elsewhere herein. All Rights Reserved. Additional Notice Provisions: [ such additional provisions, if any, as appear in the Notice in the Original Code under the heading \"Additional Notice Provisions\"]', '<<beginOptional>> SGI FREE SOFTWARE LICENSE B\n\n(Version 1.1 02/22/2000)<<endOptional>>\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Definitions.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Additional Notice Provisions\" means such additional provisions as appear in the Notice in Original Code under the heading \"Additional Notice Provisions.\"\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Covered Code\" means the Original Code or Modifications, or any combination thereof.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Hardware\" means any physical device that accepts input, processes input, stores the results of processing, and/or provides output.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Larger Work\" means a work that combines Covered Code or portions thereof with code not governed by the terms of this License.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.5\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Licensable\" means having the right to grant, to the maximum extent possible, whether at the time of the initial grant or subsequently acquired, any and all of the rights conveyed herein.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.6\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"License\" means this document.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.7\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Licensed Patents\" means patent claims Licensable by SGI that are infringed by the use or sale of Original Code or any Modifications provided by SGI, or any combination thereof.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.8\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Modifications\" means any addition to or deletion from the substance or structure of the Original Code or any previous Modifications. When Covered Code is released as a series of files, a Modification is:\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"A.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Any addition to the contents of a file containing Original Code and/or addition to or deletion from the contents of a file containing previous Modifications.\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"B.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Any new file that contains any part of the Original Code or previous Modifications.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.9\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Notice\" means any notice in Original Code or Covered Code, as required by and in compliance with this License.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.10\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Original Code\" means source code of computer software code that is described in the source code Notice required by Exhibit A as Original Code, and updates and error corrections specifically thereto.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.11\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Recipient\" means an individual or a legal entity exercising rights under, and complying with all of the terms of, this License or a future version of this License issued under Section 8. For legal entities, \"Recipient\" includes any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with Recipient. For purposes of this definition, \"control\" of an entity means (a) the power, direct or indirect, to direct or manage such entity, or (b) ownership of fifty percent (50%) or more of the outstanding shares or beneficial ownership of such entity.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.12\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Recipient Patents\" means patent claims Licensable by a Recipient that are infringed by the use or sale of Original Code or any Modifications provided by SGI, or any combination thereof.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.13\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"SGI\" means Silicon Graphics, Inc.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.14\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"SGI Patents\" means patent claims Licensable by SGI other than the Licensed Patents.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> License Grant and Restrictions.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> SGI License Grant. Subject to the terms of this License and any third party intellectual property claims, for the duration of intellectual property protections inherent in the Original Code, SGI hereby grants Recipient a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license, to do the following: (i) under copyrights Licensable by SGI, to reproduce, distribute, create derivative works from, and, to the extent applicable, display and perform the Original Code and/or any Modifications provided by SGI alone and/or as part of a Larger Work; and (ii) under any Licensable Patents, to make, have made, use, sell, offer for sale, import and/or otherwise transfer the Original Code and/or any Modifications provided by SGI. Recipient accepts the terms and conditions of this License by undertaking any of the aforementioned actions. The patent license shall apply to the Covered Code if, at the time any related Modification is added, such addition of the Modification causes such combination to be covered by the Licensed Patents. The patent license in Section 2.1(ii) shall not apply to any other combinations that include the Modification. No patent license is provided under SGI Patents for infringements of SGI Patents by Modifications not provided by SGI or combinations of Original Code and Modifications not provided by SGI.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Recipient License Grant. Subject to the terms of this License and any third party intellectual property claims, Recipient hereby grants SGI and any other Recipients a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license, under any Recipient Patents, to make, have made, use, sell, offer for sale, import and/or otherwise transfer the Original Code and/or any Modifications provided by SGI.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> No License For Hardware Implementations. The licenses granted in Section 2.1 and 2.2 are not applicable to implementation in Hardware of the algorithms embodied in the Original Code or any Modifications provided by SGI .\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Redistributions.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Retention of Notice/Copy of License. The Notice set forth in Exhibit A, below, must be conspicuously retained or included in any and all redistributions of Covered Code. For distributions of the Covered Code in source code form, the Notice must appear in every file that can include a text comments field; in executable form, the Notice and a copy of this License must appear in related documentation or collateral where the Recipient\'s rights relating to Covered Code are described. Any Additional Notice Provisions which actually appears in the Original Code must also be retained or included in any and all redistributions of Covered Code.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Alternative License. Provided that Recipient is in compliance with the terms of this License, Recipient may, so long as without derogation of any of SGI\'s rights in and to the Original Code, distribute the source code and/or executable version(s) of Covered Code under (1) this License; (2) a license identical to this License but for only such changes as are necessary in order to clarify Recipient\'s role as licensor of Modifications; and/or (3) a license of Recipient\'s choosing, containing terms different from this License, provided that the license terms include this Section 3 and Sections 4, 6, 7, 10, 12, and 13, which terms may not be modified or superseded by any other terms of such license. If Recipient elects to use any license other than this License, Recipient must make it absolutely clear that any of its terms which differ from this License are offered by Recipient alone, and not by SGI. It is emphasized that this License is a limited license, and, regardless of the license form employed by Recipient in accordance with this Section 3.2, Recipient may relicense only such rights, in Original Code and Modifications by SGI, as it has actually been granted by SGI in this License.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Indemnity. Recipient hereby agrees to indemnify SGI for any liability incurred by SGI as a result of any such alternative license terms Recipient offers.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Termination. This License and the rights granted here