识共享公共许可提供了一套标准的条款和条件，创作者和其他权利持有者可以使用这些条款和条件来共享原创作品和其他受版权约束的材料以及以下公共许可中指定的某些其他权利。以下注意事项仅供参考，并不详尽，不构成我们许可的一部分。\n\n许可人注意事项：我们的公共许可证旨在供那些被授权允许公众以版权和某些其他权利限制的方式使用材料的人使用。我们的执照是不可撤销的。许可人应阅读并理解他们选择的许可的条款和条件，然后才能应用它。许可人还应在申请我们的许可证之前确保所有必要的权利，以便公众可以按预期重复使用材料。许可方应明确标记任何不受许可约束的材料。这包括其他经CC许可的材料，或在版权例外或限制下使用的材料。对许可方的更多考虑。\n\n公众注意事项：通过使用我们的公共许可之一，许可方授予公众在特定条款和条件下使用许可材料的许可。如果由于任何原因不需要许可人的许可--例如，由于任何适用的版权例外或限制-则该使用不受许可证的监管。我们的许可证只授予版权下的许可以及许可方有权授予的某些其他权利。由于其他原因，许可材料的使用仍可能受到限制，包括因为其他人对该材料拥有版权或其他权利。许可人可以提出特殊请求，例如要求对所有更改进行标记或描述。尽管我们的许可证不要求您这样做，但我们鼓励您在合理的情况下尊重这些要求。为公众提供更多的考虑。\n\n知识共享署名-NoDerials 4.0国际公共许可证\n\n通过行使被许可的权利(定义如下)，您接受并同意受本知识共享署名-未衍生4.0国际公共许可(“公共许可”)的条款和条件的约束。在本公共许可可被解释为合同的范围内，您将被授予许可权利，作为您接受这些条款和条件的代价，许可方授予您此类权利的代价是许可方通过根据这些条款和条件提供许可材料而获得的好处。\n\n第1节--定义。\n\nA.改编材料是指受版权及类似权利约束的材料，该材料源自或基于许可材料，其中许可材料的翻译、更改、排列、转换或以其他方式修改的方式需要许可方持有的版权及类似权利的许可。就本公共许可而言，如果许可材料是音乐作品、表演或录音，则始终在许可材料与运动图像的时间关系上同步的情况下制作改编材料。\n\nB.版权和类似权利是指版权和/或与版权密切相关的类似权利，包括但不限于表演、广播、录音和独具特色的数据库权利，而不考虑权利是如何标记或分类的。就本公共许可而言，第2(B)(1)-(2)节中指定的权利不是版权和类似权利。\n\nC.有效的技术措施是指在没有适当权力的情况下，根据履行1996年12月20日通过的《WIPO著作权条约》第11条和/或类似国际协定义务的法律不得规避的措施。\n\nD.例外和限制是指公平使用、公平交易和/或适用于您对许可材料的使用的版权及类似权利的任何其他例外或限制。\n\nE.许可材料是指许可方应用本公共许可的艺术或文学作品、数据库或其他材料。\n\nF.许可权利是指根据本公共许可的条款和条件授予您的权利，这些权利仅限于适用于您使用许可材料且许可方有权许可的所有版权和类似权利。\n\n许可人是指在本公开许可项下授予权利的个人(S)或单位。\n\nH.共享是指通过复制、公开展示、公开表演、分发、传播、传播或进口等任何需要许可的方式或过程向公众提供材料，并向公众提供材料，包括公众可以在他们个人选择的地点和时间访问材料的方式。\n\nI.通用数据库权利是指欧洲议会和欧洲理事会1996年3月11日关于数据库法律保护的第96/9/EC号指令所产生的版权以外的权利，以及世界上其他实质上同等的权利。\n\nJ.您是指行使许可的个人或实体本公共许可证下的权利。你也有相应的意思。\n\n第2节--范围。\n\nA.许可证发放。\n\n1.根据本公共许可的条款和条件，许可方特此授予您全球范围内的、免版税、不可再许可、非排他性、不可撤销的许可，以行使许可材料中的许可权利，以：\n\nA.复制和分享全部或部分许可材料；以及\n\n制作和复制改编的材料，但不分享。\n\n2.例外和限制。为免生疑问，在适用于您的使用的例外和限制的情况下，本公共许可不适用，并且您不需要遵守其条款和条件。\n\n3.期限。本公共许可证的条款在第6(A)节中规定。\n\n4.媒体和格式；允许进行技术修改。许可方授权您在所有已知或今后创建的媒体和格式中行使许可权利，并进行必要的技术修改。许可方放弃且/或同意不主张任何权利或授权，以禁止您进行行使许可权利所需的技术修改，包括规避有效技术措施所需的技术修改。就本公共许可而言，仅按第2(A)(4)款授权进行修改绝不会产生改编的材料。\n\n5.下游收件人。\n\nA.许可方许可材料的报价。许可材料的每个接收者自动从许可方收到根据本公共许可的条款和条件行使许可权利的要约。\n\nB.没有下游限制。您不得对许可材料提供或强加任何附加或不同的条款或条件，或对许可材料应用任何有效的技术措施，如果这样做会限制任何公司行使许可权利许可材料的初级品。\n\n6.没有背书。本公共许可证中的任何内容都不构成或可能被解释为允许断言或暗示您与许可方或根据第3(A)(1)(A)(I)条被指定接收署名的其他人有关连，或您对许可材料的使用与许可方有关，或由许可方赞助、背书或授予正式身份。\n\nB.其他权利。\n\n1.精神权利，如完整权利，不在本公共许可下获得许可，宣传、隐私和/或其他类似的人格权利也不在本公共许可下获得许可；但是，在可能的范围内，许可方放弃和/或同意不主张许可方所拥有的任何此类权利，仅限于允许您行使许可权利所必需的程度，而不是以其他方式。\n\n2.专利权和商标权未在本公共许可下获得许可。\n\n3.在可能的范围内，许可方放弃根据任何自愿或可放弃的法定或强制许可计划直接或通过收集协会向您收取许可权利的任何权利。在所有其他情况下，许可方明确保留收取此类版税的任何权利。\n\n第3节-许可条件。\n\n您对许可权利的行使明确遵守以下条件。\n\nA.归属。\n\n1.如果您共享许可材料，则必须：\n\nA.如果许可方向许可方提供许可材料，请保留以下内容：\n\nI.以许可方要求的任何合理方式(如果指定，包括化名)识别许可材料的创建者(S)和被指定接收署名的任何其他人；\n\n二、版权声明；\n\n三、一份涉及本公共许可的通知；\n\n四、提及保证免责声明的通知；\n\nV.URI或超链接在合理可行的范围内向许可材料添加油墨；\n\nB.表明您是否修改了许可材料，并保留了先前任何修改的说明；以及\n\nC.表明许可材料是根据本公共许可证进行许可的，并包括本公共许可证的文本、URI或超链接。\n\n2.为免生疑问，根据本公共许可证，您没有共享改编材料的许可。\n\n3.您可以基于您共享许可材料的媒介、手段和环境，以任何合理的方式满足第3(A)(1)节中的条件。例如，通过提供指向包括所需信息的资源的URI或超链接来满足条件可能是合理的。\n\n4.如果许可方提出要求，您必须在合理可行的范围内删除第3(A)(1)(A)节所要求的任何信息。\n\n第4节--独有的数据库权利。\n\n如果许可权利包括适用于您使用许可材料的Sui Generis数据库权利：\n\nA.为免生疑问，第2(A)(1)条授予您摘录、重复使用、复制和共享数据库的全部或大部分内容的权利，前提是您不共享改编的材料；\n\nB.如果您将所有或大部分数据库内容包括在您拥有单独数据库权限的数据库中，则您在其中拥有单独数据库权限(但不是其个别内容)的数据库是改编材料；以及\n\nC.如果您共享数据库的全部或大部分内容，则必须遵守第3(A)节中的条件。\n为免生疑问，在许可权利包括其他版权和类似权利的情况下，本第4节是对您在本公共许可下的义务的补充，并不取代您的义务。\n\n第5节--免责声明和责任限制。\n\nA.除非另有规定由许可方单独承担，许可方尽可能按原样和原样提供许可材料，并且不对许可材料作出任何形式的陈述或保证，无论是明示的、暗示的、法定的还是其他的。这包括但不限于对所有权、适销性、特定用途的适用性、不侵权、不存在潜在或其他缺陷、准确性或错误的存在或不存在的保证，无论是否已知或可发现。如果不允许全部或部分免责声明，则本免责声明可能不适用于您。\n\nB.在可能的情况下，许可方不会因任何法律理论(包括但不限于疏忽)或其他原因，就本公共许可或许可材料的使用而产生的任何直接、特殊、间接、附带、后果性、惩罚性、惩罚性或其他损失、成本、支出或损害向您承担责任，即使许可方已被告知此类损失、成本、支出或损害的可能性。如果不允许对全部或部分责任进行限制，则此限制可能不适用于您。\n\nC.以上规定的免责声明和责任限制的解释应尽可能与绝对免责和放弃所有责任的方式最接近。\n\n第6节--任期和终止。\n\nA.本公共许可适用于在此许可的版权及类似权利的期限。但是，如果您不遵守本公共许可证，则您在本公共许可证下的权利将自动终止。\n\nB.如果您使用许可材料的权利已根据第6(A)条终止，则恢复：\n\n1.自违规行为被纠正之日起自动生效，前提是该违规行为在您发现违规行为后30天内被纠正；或\n\n2.在许可方明示恢复时。\n\nC.为避免停工BT，本第6(B)条不影响许可方可能就您违反本公共许可的行为寻求补救的任何权利。\n\nD.为免生疑问，许可方还可以根据单独的条款或条件提供许可材料，或随时停止分发许可材料；但是，这样做并不会终止本公共许可。\n\nE.第1、5、6、7和8节在本公共许可终止后继续生效。\n\n第7节--其他条款和条件。\n\nA.除非明确同意，许可方不受您传达的任何附加或不同条款或条件的约束。\n\nB.此处未说明的关于许可材料的任何安排、谅解或协议均独立于本公共许可的条款和条件。\n\n第8节--释义。\n\nA.为免生疑问，本《公共许可证》不会、也不应解释为减少、限制、限制或对未经本《公共许可证》许可而合法使用许可材料施加任何条件。\n\nB.在可能的范围内，如果本公共许可证的任何规定被认为是不可执行的，应自动进行改革，使其达到可强制执行的最低必要程度。如果不能修改该条款，则应将其从本公共许可中移除，但不影响其余条款和条件的可执行性。\n\nC.除非许可方明确同意，否则不会放弃本公共许可的任何条款或条件，也不会同意不遵守。\n\nD.本公共许可证中的任何内容均不构成或可解释为限制或放弃适用于许可方或您的任何特权和豁免，包括任何司法管辖区或当局的法律程序。\n\nCreative Commons不是其公共许可证的缔约方。尽管如此，知识共享可能会选择将其公共许可证之一应用于其发布的材料在这些情况下，将被视为“许可方”。除非出于表明材料是在知识共享公共许可下共享的有限目的，或在creativeommons.org/策略上发布的知识共享政策另有允许，否则在没有事先书面同意的情况下，知识共享不授权使用“知识共享”商标或知识共享的任何其他商标或徽标，包括但不限于对其任何公共许可的任何未经授权的修改或与使用许可材料有关的任何其他安排、谅解或协议。为免生疑问，本段不构成公共许可的一部分。\n\n知识共享可以在creativeommons.org上联系。', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (281, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'CDLA-Permissive-1.0', 'Community Data License Agreement Permissive 1.0', 'https://cdla.io/permissive-1-0', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> Community Data License Agreement - Permissive - Version 1.0<<endOptional>>\n\nThis is the Community Data License Agreement - Permissive, Version 1.0 (\"Agreement\"). Data is provided to You under this Agreement by each of the Data Providers. Your exercise of any of the rights and permissions granted below constitutes Your acceptance and agreement to be bound by the terms and conditions of this Agreement.\n\nThe benefits that each Data Provider receives from making Data available and that You receive from Data or otherwise under these terms and conditions shall be deemed sufficient consideration for the formation of this Agreement. Accordingly, Data Provider(s) and You (the \"Parties\") agree as follows:\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Section 1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Definitions\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Add\" means to supplement Data with Your own or someone else\'s Data, resulting in Your \"Additions.\" Additions do not include Results.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Computational Use\" means Your analysis (through the use of computational devices or otherwise) or other interpretation of Data. By way of example and not limitation, \"Computational Use\" includes the application of any computational analytical technique, the purpose of which is the analysis of any Data in digital form to generate information about Data such as patterns, trends, correlations, inferences, insights and attributes.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Data\" means the information (including copyrightable information, such as images or text), collectively or individually, whether created or gathered by a Data Provider or an Entity acting on its behalf, to which rights are granted under this Agreement.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Data Provider\" means any Entity (including any employee or contractor of such Entity authorized to Publish Data on behalf of such Entity) that Publishes Data under this Agreement prior to Your Receiving it.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.5\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Enhanced Data\" means the subset of Data that You Publish and that is composed of (a) Your Additions and/or (b) Modifications to Data You have received under this Agreement.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.6\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Entity\" means any natural person or organization that exists under the laws of the jurisdiction in which it is organized, together with all other entities that control, are controlled by, or are under common control with that entity. For the purposes of this definition, \"control\" means (a) the power, directly or indirectly, to cause the direction or management of such entity, whether by contract or otherwise, (b) the ownership of more than fifty percent (50%) of the outstanding shares or securities, (c) the beneficial ownership of such entity or, (d) the ability to appoint, whether by agreement or right, the majority of directors of an Entity.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.7\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Modify\" means to delete, erase, correct or re-arrange Data, resulting in \"Modifications.\" Modifications do not include Results.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.8\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Publish\" means to make all or a subset of Data (including Your Enhanced Data) available in any manner which enables its Use, including by providing a copy on physical media or remote access. For any form of Entity, that is to make the Data available to any individual who is not employed by that Entity or engaged as a contractor or agent to perform work on that Entity\'s behalf. A \"Publication\" occurs each time You Publish Data.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.9\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Receive\" or \"Receives\" means to have been given access to Data, locally or remotely.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.10\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Results\" means the outcomes or outputs that You obtain from Your Computational Use of Data. Results shall not include more than a de minimis portion of the Data on which the Computational Use is based.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.11\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Sui Generis Database Rights\" means rights, other than copyright, resulting from Directive 96/9/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 March 1996 on the legal protection of databases, as amended and/or succeeded, as well as other equivalent rights anywhere in the world.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.12\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"Use\" means using Data (including accessing, copying, studying, reviewing, adapting, analyzing, evaluating, or making Computational Use of it), either by machines or humans, or a combination of both.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"1.13\";match=\".{0,20}\">> \"You\" or \"Your\" means any Entity that Receives Data under this Agreement.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Section 2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Right and License to Use and to Publish\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Subject to the conditions set forth in Section 3 of this Agreement, Data Provider(s) hereby grant(s) to You a worldwide, non-exclusive, irrevocable (except as provided in Section 5) right to: (a) Use Data; and (b) Publish Data.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> To the extent that the Data or the coordination, selection or arrangement of Data is protected or protectable under copyright, Sui Generis Database Rights, or other law, Data Provider(s) further agree(s) that such Data or coordination, selection or arrangement is hereby licensed to You and to anyone else who Receives Data under this Agreement for Use and Publication, subject to the conditions set forth in Section 3 of this Agreement.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"2.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Except for these rights and licenses expressly granted, no other intellectual property rights are granted or should be implied.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Section 3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Conditions on Rights Granted\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> If You Publish Data You Receive or Enhanced Data:\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"(a)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may do so under a license of Your choice provided that You give anyone who Receives the Data from You the text of this Agreement, the name of this Agreement and/or a hyperlink or other method reasonably likely to provide a copy of the text of this Agreement; and\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"(b)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You must cause any Data files containing Enhanced Data to carry prominent notices that You have changed those files; and\n\n         <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"(c)\";match=\".{0,20}\">> If You Publish Data You Receive, You must preserve all credit or attribution to the Data Provider(s). Such retained credit or attribution includes any of the following to the extent they exist in Data as You have Received it: legal notices or metadata; identification of the Data Provider(s); or hyperlinks to Data to the extent it is practical to do so.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You may provide additional or different license terms and conditions for use, reproduction, or distribution of that Enhanced Data, or for any combination of Data and Enhanced Data as a whole, provided that Your Use and Publication of that combined Data otherwise complies with the conditions stated in this License.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You and each Data Provider agree that Enhanced Data shall not be considered a work of joint authorship by virtue of its relationship to Data licensed under this Agreement and shall not require either any obligation of accounting to or the consent of any Data Provider.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"3.4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Agreement imposes no obligations or restrictions on Your Use or Publication of Results.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Section 4.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Data Provider(s)\' Representations\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"4.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Each Data Provider represents that the Data Provider has exercised reasonable care, to assure that: (a) the Data it Publishes was created or generated by it or was obtained from others with the right to Publish the Data under this Agreement; and (b) Publication of such Data does not violate any privacy or confidentiality obligation undertaken by the Data Provider.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Section 5.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Termination\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> All of Your rights under this Agreement will terminate, and Your right to Receive, Use or Publish the Data will be revoked or modified if You materially fail to comply with the terms and conditions of this Agreement and You do not cure such failure in a reasonable period of time after becoming aware of such noncompliance. If Your rights under this Agreement terminate, You agree to cease Receipt, Use and Publication of Data. However, Your obligations and any rights and permissions granted by You under this Agreement relating to Data that You Published prior to such termination will continue and survive.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"5.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> If You institute litigation against a Data Provider or anyone else who Receives the Data (including a cross-claim in a lawsuit) based on the Data, other than a claim asserting breach of this Agreement, then any rights previously granted to You to Receive, Use and Publish Data under this Agreement will terminate as of the date such litigation is filed.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Section 6.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Disclaimer of Warranties and Limitation of Liability\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> EXCEPT AS EXPRESSLY SET FORTH IN THIS AGREEMENT, THE DATA (INCLUDING ENHANCED DATA) IS PROVIDED ON AN \"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, ANY WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, MERCHANTABILITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"6.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> NEITHER YOU NOR ANY DATA PROVIDERS SHALL HAVE ANY LIABILITY FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION LOST PROFITS), HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OR DISTRIBUTION OF THE DATA OR THE EXERCISE OF ANY RIGHTS GRANTED HEREUNDER, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Section 7.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Miscellaneous\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.1\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You agree that it is solely Your responsibility to comply with all applicable laws with regard to Your Use or Publication of Data, including any applicable privacy, data protection, security and export laws. You agree to take reasonable steps to assist a Data Provider fulfilling responsibilities to comply with applicable laws with regard to Use or Publication of Data Received hereunder.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.2\";match=\".{0,20}\">> You and Data Provider(s), collectively and individually, waive and/or agree not to assert, to the extent permitted by law, any moral rights You or they hold in Data.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.3\";match=\".{0,20}\">> This Agreement confers no rights or remedies upon any person or entity other than the Parties and their respective heirs, executors, successors and assigns.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.4\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Data Provider(s) reserve no right or expectation of privacy, data protection or confidentiality in any Data that they Publish under this Agreement. If You choose to Publish Data under this Agreement, You similarly do so with no reservation or expectation of any rights of privacy or confidentiality in that Data.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"7.5\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Community Data License Agreement workgroup under The Linux Foundation is the steward of this Agreement (\"Steward\"). No one other than the Steward has the right to modify or publish new versions of this Agreement. Each version will be given a distinguishing version number. You may Use and Publish Data Received hereunder under the terms of the version of the Agreement under which You originally Received the Data, or under the terms of any subsequent version published by the Steward.', 'Community Data License Agreement – Permissive – Version 1.0\n\nThis is the Community Data License Agreement – Permissive, Version 1.0 (“Agreement”).  Data is provided to You under this Agreement by each of the Data Providers.  Your exercise of any of the rights and permissions granted below constitutes Your acceptance and agreement to be bound by the terms and conditions of this Agreement.\n\nThe benefits that each Data Provider receives from making Data available and that You receive from Data or otherwise under these terms and conditions shall be deemed sufficient consideration for the formation of this Agreement.  Accordingly, Data Provider(s) and You (the “Parties”) agree as follows:\n\nSection 1.  Definitions\n\n1.1 “Add” means to supplement Data with Your own or someone else’s Data, resulting in Your “Additions.”  Additions do not include Results.\n\n1.2 “Computational Use” means Your analysis (through the use of computational devices or otherwise) or other interpretation of Data.  By way of example and not limitation, “Computational Use” includes the application of any computational analytical technique, the purpose of which is the analysis of any Data in digital form to generate information about Data such as patterns, trends, correlations, inferences, insights and attributes.\n\n1.3 “Data” means the information (including copyrightable information, such as images or text), collectively or individually, whether created or gathered by a Data Provider or an Entity acting on its behalf, to which rights are granted under this Agreement.\n\n1.4 “Data Provider” means any Entity (including any employee or contractor of such Entity authorized to Publish Data on behalf of such Entity) that Publishes Data under this Agreement prior to Your Receiving it.\n\n1.5 “Enhanced Data” means the subset of Data that You Publish and that is composed of (a) Your Additions and/or (b) Modifications to Data You have received under this Agreement.\n\n1.6 “Entity” means any natural person or organization that exists under the laws of the jurisdiction in which it is organized, together with all other entities that control, are controlled by, or are under common control with that entity.  For the purposes of this definition, “control” means (a) the power, directly or indirectly, to cause the direction or management of such entity, whether by contract or otherwise, (b) the ownership of more than fifty percent (50%) of the outstanding shares or securities, (c) the beneficial ownership of such entity or, (d) the ability to appoint, whether by agreement or right, the majority of directors of an Entity.\n\n1.7 “Modify” means to delete, erase, correct or re-arrange Data, resulting in “Modifications.”  Modifications do not include Results.\n\n1.8 “Publish” means to make all or a subset of Data (including Your Enhanced Data) available in any manner which enables its Use, including by providing a copy on physical media or remote access.  For any form of Entity, that is to make the Data available to any individual who is not employed by that Entity or engaged as a contractor or agent to perform work on that Entity’s behalf.  A “Publication” occurs each time You Publish Data.\n\n1.9 “Receive” or “Receives” means to have been given access to Data, locally or remotely.\n\n1.10 “Results” means the outcomes or outputs that You obtain from Your Computational Use of Data.  Results shall not include more than a de minimis portion of the Data on which the Computational Use is based.\n\n1.11 “Sui Generis Database Rights” means rights, other than copyright, resulting from Directive 96/9/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 March 1996 on the legal protection of databases, as amended and/or succeeded, as well as other equivalent rights anywhere in the world.\n\n1.12 “Use” means using Data (including accessing, copying, studying, reviewing, adapting, analyzing, evaluating, or making Computational Use of it), either by machines or humans, or a combination of both.\n\n1.13 “You” or “Your” means any Entity that Receives Data under this Agreement.\n\nSection 2.  Right and License to Use and to Publish\n\n2.1 Subject to the conditions set forth in Section 3 of this Agreement, Data Provider(s) hereby grant(s) to You a worldwide, non-exclusive, irrevocable (except as provided in Section 5) right to: (a) Use Data; and (b) Publish Data.\n\n2.2 To the extent that the Data or the coordination, selection or arrangement of Data is protected or protectable under copyright, Sui Generis Database Rights, or other law, Data Provider(s) further agree(s) that such Data or coordination, selection or arrangement is hereby licensed to You and to anyone else who Receives Data under this Agreement for Use and Publication, subject to the conditions set forth in Section 3 of this Agreement.\n\n2.3 Except for these rights and licenses expressly granted, no other intellectual property rights are granted or should be implied.\n\nSection 3.  Conditions on Rights Granted\n\n3.1 If You Publish Data You Receive or Enhanced Data:\n\n(a) You may do so under a license of Your choice provided that You give anyone who Receives the Data from You the text of this Agreement, the name of this Agreement and/or a hyperlink or other method reasonably likely to provide a copy of the text of this Agreement; and\n\n(b) You must cause any Data files containing Enhanced Data to carry prominent notices that You have changed those files; and\n\n(c) If You Publish Data You Receive, You must preserve all credit or attribution to the Data Provider(s). Such retained credit or attribution includes any of the following to the extent they exist in Data as You have Received it: legal notices or metadata; identification of the Data Provider(s); or hyperlinks to Data to the extent it is practical to do so.\n\n3.2 You may provide additional or different license terms and conditions for use, reproduction, or distribution of that Enhanced Data, or for any combination of Data and Enhanced Data as a whole, provided that Your Use and Publication of that combined Data otherwise complies with the conditions stated in this License.\n\n3.3 You and each Data Provider agree that Enhanced Data shall not be considered a work of joint authorship by virtue of its relationship to Data licensed under this Agreement and shall not require either any obligation of accounting to or the consent of any Data Provider.\n\n3.4 This Agreement imposes no obligations or restrictions on Your Use or Publication of Results.\n\nSection 4.  Data Provider(s)’ Representations\n\n4.1 Each Data Provider represents that the Data Provider has exercised reasonable care, to assure that: (a) the Data it Publishes was created or generated by it or was obtained from others with the right to Publish the Data under this Agreement; and (b) Publication of such Data does not violate any privacy or confidentiality obligation undertaken by the Data Provider.\n\nSection 5.  Termination\n\n5.1 All of Your rights under this Agreement will terminate, and Your right to Receive, Use or Publish the Data will be revoked or modified if You materially fail to comply with the terms and conditions of this Agreement and You do not cure such failure in a reasonable period of time after becoming aware of such noncompliance.  If Your rights under this Agreement terminate, You agree to cease Receipt, Use and Publication of Data.  However, Your obligations and any rights and permissions granted by You under this Agreement relating to Data that You Published prior to such termination will continue and survive.\n\n5.2 If You institute litigation against a Data Provider or anyone else who Receives the Data (including a cross-claim in a lawsuit) based on the Data, other than a claim asserting breach of this Agreement, then any rights previously granted to You to Receive, Use and Publish Data under this Agreement will terminate as of the date such litigation is filed.\n\nSection 6.  Disclaimer of Warranties and Limitation of Liability\n\n6.1 EXCEPT AS EXPRESSLY SET FORTH IN THIS AGREEMENT, THE DATA (INCLUDING ENHANCED DATA) IS PROVIDED ON AN “AS IS” BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, ANY WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, MERCHANTABILITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.\n\n6.2 NEITHER YOU NOR ANY DATA PROVIDERS SHALL HAVE ANY LIABILITY FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION LOST PROFITS), HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OR DISTRIBUTION OF THE DATA OR THE EXERCISE OF ANY RIGHTS GRANTED HEREUNDER, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.\n\nSection 7.  Miscellaneous\n\n7.1 You agree that it is solely Your responsibility to comply with all applicable laws with regard to Your Use or Publication of Data, including any applicable privacy, data protection, security and export laws.  You agree to take reasonable steps to assist a Data Provider fulfilling responsibilities to comply with applicable laws with regard to Use or Publication of Data Received hereunder.\n\n7.2 You and Data Provider(s), collectively and individually, waive and/or agree not to assert, to the extent permitted by law, any moral rights You or they hold in Data.\n\n7.3 This Agreement confers no rights or remedies upon any person or entity other than the Parties and their respective heirs, executors, successors and assigns.\n\n7.4 The Data Provider(s) reserve no right or expectation of privacy, data protection or confidentiality in any Data that they Publish under this Agreement.  If You choose to Publish Data under this Agreement, You similarly do so with no reservation or expectation of any rights of privacy or confidentiality in that Data.\n\n7.5 The Community Data License Agreement workgroup under The Linux Foundation is the steward of this Agreement (“Steward”).  No one other than the Steward has the right to modify or publish new versions of this Agreement.  Each version will be given a distinguishing version number.  You may Use and Publish Data Received hereunder under the terms of the version of the Agreement under which You originally Received the Data, or under the terms of any subsequent version published by the Steward.', '社区数据许可协议-许可-版本1.0\n\n这是社区数据许可协议-许可，版本1.0(“协议”)。数据提供商根据本协议向您提供数据。您行使以下授予的任何权利和许可，即表示您接受并同意受本协议的条款和条件约束。\n\n每个数据提供商从提供数据中获得的利益，以及您根据这些条款和条件从数据或其他方面获得的利益，应被视为形成本协议的充分对价。因此，数据提供者(S)和您(“当事人”)同意如下：\n\n第1节.定义\n\n1.1“添加”是指用自己或他人的数据来补充数据，从而导致您的“添加”。添加不包括结果。\n\n1.2“计算性使用”是指您对数据的分析(通过使用计算设备或其他方式)或其他解释。作为例子而非限制，“计算使用”包括任何计算分析技术的应用，其目的是以数字形式分析任何数据，以产生关于数据的信息，如模式、趋势、相关性、推论、见解和属性。\n\n1.3“数据”是指根据本协议授予权利的信息(包括图像或文本等可受版权保护的信息)，无论是由数据提供商或代表其行事的实体创建或收集的。\n\n1.4“数据提供者”是指在您收到数据之前根据本协议发布数据的任何实体(包括被授权代表该实体发布数据的该实体的任何雇员或承包商)。\n\n1.5“增强型数据”是指您发布的数据子集，由(A)您根据本协议获得的数据的补充和/或修改组成。\n\n1.6“实体”是指任何自然人或组织N根据其组织所在管辖区的法律存在的实体，以及控制该实体、受该实体控制或与该实体共同控制的所有其他实体。在本定义中，“控制”是指(A)以合同或其他方式直接或间接导致对该实体进行指挥或管理的权力，(B)超过50%(50%)的流通股或证券的所有权，(C)该实体的实益所有权，或(D)以协议或权利任命该实体的多数董事的能力。\n\n1.7“修改”是指删除、擦除、更正或重新排列数据，从而导致“修改”。修改不包括结果。\n\n1.8“发布”是指以任何方式提供所有或部分数据(包括您的增强型数据)，包括在物理媒体上提供副本或远程访问。对于任何形式的实体，即向没有受雇于该实体或作为承包人或代理人受雇代表该实体执行工作的任何个人提供数据。每次发布数据时，都会发生一次“发布”。\n\n1.9“接收”或“接收”意味着已获得本地或远程访问数据的权限。\n\n1.10“结果”是指您通过计算使用数据而获得的结果或输出。结果不应包括作为计算使用依据的数据的最小部分。\n\n1.11“特殊数据库权利”系指欧洲议会和欧洲理事会1996年3月11日关于数据库法律保护的第96/9/EC号指令所产生的权利，版权除外，以及世界上任何地方的其他同等权利。\n\n1.12“使用”是指通过机器或人类或两者的组合使用数据(包括访问、复制、研究、审查、改编、分析、评估或计算使用)。\n\n1.13“你”或“你的”“指根据本协议接收数据的任何实体。\n\n第2节使用和发布的权利和许可证\n\n2.1在符合本协议第3节规定的条件下，数据提供商(S)特此授予(S)全球范围内的、非排他性的、不可撤销的(第5节规定的除外)权利：(A)使用数据；和(B)发布数据。\n\n2.2在数据或数据的协调、选择或安排受著作权、特殊数据库权利或其他法律保护或保护的范围内，数据提供商(S)进一步同意(S)，此类数据或数据的协调、选择或安排在此许可给您和根据本协议接收数据的任何其他人以供使用和发布，但须遵守本协议第3节规定的条件。\n\n2.3除这些明确授予的权利和许可外，不授予或不应默示任何其他知识产权。\n\n第三节关于授予权利的条件\n\n3.1如果您发布数据，则会收到或增强数据：\n\n(A)您可以在您选择的许可下这样做，前提是您向从您收到数据的任何人提供本协议文本、本协议名称和/或超链接或其他合理可能提供本协议文本副本的方法；和\n\n(B)您必须使任何包含增强数据的数据文件带有您已更改这些文件的显眼通知；以及\n\n(C)如果您发布您收到的数据，您必须保留数据提供者的所有信用或归属(S)。此类保留的信用或归属包括以下任何内容：法律通知或元数据；数据提供者的身份(S)；或实际可行的数据超链接。\n\n3.2您可以为增强数据的使用、复制或分发提供附加或不同的许可条款和条件，或作为一个整体为数据和增强数据的任何组合提供附加或不同的许可条款和条件，前提是您使用和该合并数据的发布在其他方面符合本许可证中规定的条件。\n\n3.3您和每个数据提供商同意，增强数据不应因其与根据本协议许可的数据的关系而被视为合作作品，并且不需要向任何数据提供商承担任何会计义务或征得任何数据提供商的同意。\n\n3.4本协议不对您使用或发布结果施加任何义务或限制。\n\n第四节数据提供者(S)的陈述\n\n4.1每一数据提供商均表示，数据提供商已采取合理的谨慎措施，以保证：(A)其发布的数据是由其创建或生成的，或从有权根据本协议发布数据的其他人处获得；以及(B)发布此类数据不违反数据提供商承担的任何隐私或保密义务。\n\n第5节.终止\n\n5.1如果您严重违反本协议的条款和条件，并且您在意识到此类不遵守行为后没有在合理的时间内纠正该错误，则您在本协议项下的所有权利将终止，您接收、使用或发布数据的权利将被撤销或修改。如果您在本协议下的权利终止，您同意停止接收、使用和发布数据。但是，您在本协议下授予的有关您在终止之前发布的数据的义务以及任何权利和许可将继续存在。\n\n5.2如果您根据数据对数据提供商或任何其他收到数据的人提起诉讼(包括诉讼中的交叉索赔)，但声称违反本协议的索赔除外，则以前根据本协议授予您的接收、使用和发布数据的任何权利将自提起诉讼之日起终止。\n\n第6节免责声明和责任限制\n\n6.1除本协议明文规定外根据协议，数据(包括增强数据)是以“原样”为基础提供的，没有任何明示或默示的担保或条件，包括但不限于所有权、不侵权、适销性或对特定目的的适用性的任何担保或条件。\n\n6.2对于任何直接、间接、附带、特殊、惩罚性或后果性的损害(包括但不限于利润损失)，您和任何数据提供商都不承担任何责任，无论这些损害是由合同、严格责任或侵权(包括疏忽或其他)责任理论引起的，即使被告知此类损害的可能性也是如此。\n\n第7节杂项\n\n7.1您同意，遵守与您使用或发布数据有关的所有适用法律，包括任何适用的隐私、数据保护、安全和出口法律，完全是您的责任。您同意采取合理步骤，协助数据提供商履行在使用或发布本协议下收到的数据方面遵守适用法律的责任。\n\n7.2您和数据提供商(S)集体和单独放弃和/或同意在法律允许的范围内不主张您或他们在数据中拥有的任何精神权利。\n\n7.3除当事各方及其各自的继承人、遗嘱执行人、继承人和受让人外，本协议不赋予任何个人或实体任何权利或救济。\n\n7.4数据提供商(S)对他们根据本协议发布的任何数据不保留任何隐私、数据保护或保密的权利或期望。如果您选择根据本协议发布数据，您同样可以在不保留或期望对该数据享有任何隐私权或保密权的情况下这样做。\n\n7.5 Linux基金会下属的社区数据许可协议工作组是本协议的管理人员(“管理人员”)。没有别人，只有管家有权修改或发布本协议的新版本。每个版本都会有一个不同的版本号。您可以根据您最初收到数据时所依据的协议版本的条款，或根据管理人员发布的任何后续版本的条款，使用和发布在本协议下收到的数据。', NULL);
INSERT INTO `license` VALUES (282, '2023-05-11 23:28:24', 'CC-BY-NC-4.0', 'Creative Commons Attribution Non Commercial 4.0 International', 'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, '<<beginOptional>> <<beginOptional>> Creative Commons<<endOptional>> Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International<<endOptional>><<beginOptional>> Creative Commons Corporation (\"Creative Commons\") is not a law firm and does not provide legal services or legal advice. Distribution of Creative Commons public licenses does not create a lawyer-client or other relationship. Creative Commons makes its licenses and related information available on an \"as-is\" basis. Creative Commons gives no warranties regarding its licenses, any material licensed under their terms and conditions, or any related information. Creative Commons disclaims all liability for damages resulting from their use to the fullest extent possible.\n\nUsing Creative Commons Public Licenses\n\nCreative Commons public licenses provide a standard set of terms and conditions that creators and other rights holders may use to share original works of authorship and other material subject to copyright and certain other rights specified in the public license below. The following considerations are for informational purposes only, are not exhaustive, and do not form part of our licenses.\n\n   \n\n   Considerations for licensors: Our public licenses are intended for use by those authorized to give the public permission to use material in ways otherwise restricted by copyright and certain other rights. Our licenses are irrevocable. Licensors should read and understand the terms and conditions of the license they choose before applying it. Licensors should also secure all rights necessary before applying our licenses so that the public can reuse the material as expected. Licensors should clearly mark any material not subject to the license. This includes other CC-licensed material, or material used under an exception or limitation to copyright. More considerations for licensors <<var;name=\"considerationsLicensors\";original=\": wiki.creativecommons.org/Considerations_for_licensors\";match=\": wiki.creativecommons.org/Considerations_for_licensors|\\.\">>\n\n   \n\n   Considerations for the public: By using one of our public licenses, a licensor grants the public permission to use the licensed material under specified terms and conditions. If the licensor\'s permission is not necessary for any reason–for example, because of any applicable exception or limitation to copyright–then that use is not regulated by the license. Our licenses grant only permissions under copyright and certain other rights that a licensor has authority to grant. Use of the licensed material may still be restricted for other reasons, including because others have copyright or other rights in the material. A licensor may make special requests, such as asking that all changes be marked or described. Although not required by our licenses, you are encouraged to respect those requests where reasonable. <<var;name=\"spaceUnderscore\";original=\"More considerations\";match=\"More considerations|More_considerations\">> for the public <<var;name=\"considerationsLicensees\";original=\": wiki.creativecommons.org/Considerations_for_licensees\";match=\": wiki.creativecommons.org/Considerations_for_licensees|\\.\">><<endOptional>><<beginOptional>> Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International Public License<<endOptional>>\n\nBy exercising the Licensed Rights (defined below), You accept and agree to be bound by the terms and conditions of this Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International Public License (\"Public License\"). To the extent this Public License may be interpreted as a contract, You are granted the Licensed Rights in consideration of Your acceptance of these terms and conditions, and the Licensor grants You such rights in consideration of benefits the Licensor receives from making the Licensed Material available under these terms and conditions.\n\n   \n\n   Section 1 – Definitions.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"a.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Adapted Material means material subject to Copyright and Similar Rights that is derived from or based upon the Licensed Material and in which the Licensed Material is translated, altered, arranged, transformed, or otherwise modified in a manner requiring permission under the Copyright and Similar Rights held by the Licensor. For purposes of this Public License, where the Licensed Material is a musical work, performance, or sound recording, Adapted Material is always produced where the Licensed Material is synched in timed relation with a moving image.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"b.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Adapter\'s License means the license You apply to Your Copyright and Similar Rights in Your contributions to Adapted Material in accordance with the terms and conditions of this Public License.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"c.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Copyright and Similar Rights means copyright and/or similar rights closely related to copyright including, without limitation, performance, broadcast, sound recording, and Sui Generis Database Rights, without regard to how the rights are labeled or categorized. For purposes of this Public License, the rights specified in Section 2(b)(1)-(2) are not Copyright and Similar Rights.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"d.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Effective Technological Measures means those measures that, in the absence of proper authority, may not be circumvented under laws fulfilling obligations under Article 11 of the WIPO Copyright Treaty adopted on December 20, 1996, and/or similar international agreements.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"e.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Exceptions and Limitations means fair use, fair dealing, and/or any other exception or limitation to Copyright and Similar Rights that applies to Your use of the Licensed Material.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"f.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Licensed Material means the artistic or literary work, database, or other material to which the Licensor applied this Public License.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"g.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Licensed Rights means the rights granted to You subject to the terms and conditions of this Public License, which are limited to all Copyright and Similar Rights that apply to Your use of the Licensed Material and that the Licensor has authority to license.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"h.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Licensor means the individual(s) or entity(ies) granting rights under this Public License.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"i.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> NonCommercial means not primarily intended for or directed towards commercial advantage or monetary compensation. For purposes of this Public License, the exchange of the Licensed Material for other material subject to Copyright and Similar Rights by digital file-sharing or similar means is NonCommercial provided there is no payment of monetary compensation in connection with the exchange.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"j.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Share means to provide material to the public by any means or process that requires permission under the Licensed Rights, such as reproduction, public display, public performance, distribution, dissemination, communication, or importation, and to make material available to the public including in ways that members of the public may access the material from a place and at a time individually chosen by them.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"k.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Sui Generis Database Rights means rights other than copyright resulting from Directive 96/9/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 March 1996 on the legal protection of databases, as amended and/or succeeded, as well as other essentially equivalent rights