ny reason whatsoever, shall not cause the Agreement as a whole to be null and void.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"11.5.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> LANGUAGE\n\n      The Agreement is drafted in both French and English. In the event of a conflict as regards construction, the French version shall be deemed authentic.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Article 12 -\";match=\".{0,20}\">> NEW VERSIONS OF THE AGREEMENT\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"12.1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Any or all person is authorized to duplicate and distribute copies of this Agreement.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"12.2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> So as to ensure coherence, the wording of this Agreement is protected and may only be modified by the authors of the License, that reserve the right to periodically publish updates or new versions of the Agreement, each with a separate number. These subsequent versions may address new issues encountered by Free Software.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"12.3.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> Any or all Software distributed under a given version of the Agreement may only be subsequently distributed under the same version of the Agreement, or a subsequent version, subject to the provisions of article 5.3.4.\n\n   <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"Article 13 -\";match=\".{0,20}\">> GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"13.1.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> The Agreement is governed by French law. The Parties agree to endeavor to settle the disagreements or disputes that may arise during the performance of the Agreement out-of-court.\n\n      <<var;name=\"bullet\";original=\"13.2.\";match=\".{0,20}\">> In the absence of an out-of-court settlement within two (2) months as from their occurrence, and unless emergency proceedings are necessary, the disagreements or disputes shall be referred to the Paris Courts having jurisdiction, by the first Party to take action.\n\nVersion 1.1 of 10/26/2004', 'FREE SOFTWARE 